* Grendel eggs hatch either sex, standard or Bony (openc2e Creatures 2
* project, our own scripts). Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions
* folder); safe to repeat.
*
* Grendels come from two kinds of egg, and both always hatched a male from
* the game's own grendel genome ("gren"):
* - the egg pile (2 5 4, up to 20 by x 7020), whose keeper (2 1 52) starts an
*   egg hatching when there are no grendels;
* - the egg machine by the volcano (2 1 25), which lays a grendel egg (2 5 3,
*   genome and sex in its ov00 and ov01) when there are ettins already, and
*   an ettin egg when there are none.
* The owner asked (2026-11-10) for grendel eggs to hatch, at random, a male
* or female, standard or Bony grendel (the Boney Grendels pack's genome
* "bone", from the player's own Genetics folder; the pack's mating script,
* the Bony Grendel Update, is built in through builtin-cobs.txt). These two
* hatching scripts replace the eggs' own timer scripts; the keeper and the
* machine are unchanged. Ettin eggs (also from the machine) hatch a male or
* female at random too (owner, 2026-11-10; they were always male).
*
* The egg pile's egg: pictures 0-2 while it waits (each step a random 3-6 s
* apart once started), 3-9 cracking, 10 the empty shell, gone at 11.
scrp 2 5 4 9
  doif pose ge 10
    doif pose eq 11 kill ownr stop endi
    pose 11 tick 200 stop
  endi
  doif pose lt 3
    setv var0 pose addv var0 1 pose var0
    rndv var0 30 60 tick var0 stop
  endi
  tick 0
* (the world's limit, which counts every creature: wait while it is full,
* as the game's norn eggs do; EGGL is the limit less the grendels and ettins
* alive, so this compares all creatures with it; owner, 2026-11-16)
  doif totl 4 1 0 ge eggl tick 1200 stop endi
  rndv var0 0 1
  doif var0 eq 0
    new: gene tokn gren tokn gren var4
  else
    new: gene tokn bone tokn bone var4
  endi
  rndv var3 1 2
  snde crak
  anim [34563456345634563456] over
  wait 20
  anim [3456778899] over
  setv var0 posl setv var1 posy
  inst new: crea var4 var3 drea 1 mvto var0 var1 slim setv grav 1
  targ ownr pose 10 tick 200
endm
*
* The egg machine's egg: pictures 3-6 rocking and cracking, 7 the empty
* shell. A grendel egg is made a Bony one half the time; grendel and ettin
* eggs alike hatch either sex. The machine's eggs have OV01 1 (the gene
* splicer's eggs, of the same class, leave it 0), and it lays a grendel egg
* only while there are ettins (with none, an ettin egg). OV00 can't tell
* them apart: since NEW: GENE works (2026-11-12) it holds each egg's own new
* genome, not "gren" or "ettn".
scrp 2 5 3 9
  tick 0
  doif pose eq 7 kill ownr stop endi
* (the world's limit, as the grendel eggs above)
  doif totl 4 1 0 ge eggl tick 1200 stop endi
  doif ov01 eq 1
    setv var0 0 enum 4 3 0 addv var0 1 next
    doif var0 gt 0
      rndv var0 0 1
      doif var0 eq 1 new: gene tokn bone tokn bone ov00 endi
    endi
  endi
  rndv var0 1 2 setv ov01 var0
  anim [3456543R] wait 50
  snde crak
  anim [345634563456] over
  pose 7
  setv var1 posx setv var2 post addv var2 10
  inst new: crea ov00 ov01 drea 1 mvto var1 var2 slim setv grav 1
  targ ownr tick 200
endm
